# THE SHEET TREE STAYS LOCAL EXCEPT THE MAP (2026-08-20). The video is
# big and private; sheet.map is small, hand-verified and the one thing a
# checkpoint carries, so a clone keeps the map and the jump works again
# as soon as that clone's own copy of the video is in place. (A trimmed
# `sheet.webm` and a `sheet/src/` original were listed here until
# 2026-08-20; nothing is trimmed any more and the layout is flat.)
#
# TWO THINGS ABOUT THE PATTERN. It ignores the folder's CHILDREN rather
# than the folder itself, because git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY and a `sheet/` line would make the negation unreachable. And
# it is RECURSIVE (`**`) because a piece may sit anywhere below
# `projects/` — `projects/category/piece/` is a supported shape, and it
# is the same recursive domain the history walk's own
# `:(glob)projects/**/<base>.<ext>` pathspecs use, so the privacy rule
# and the walk agree about where a project can be.
projects/**/sheet/*
!projects/**/sheet/sheet.map
projects/*test
